∈ x} is large; normal = every selector f(x) ∈ x on a large set has a large fibre; strong compactness = every κ-complete filter extends to a κ-complete ultrafilter.", "fixed_by": "def-lc-fine-ultrafilters-strong-compactness-and-supercompactness", "matters_for": ["thm-lc-strong-compactness-fine-measures-and-logic", "lem-lc-fine-ultrapower-seed-and-normality", "thm-lc-strong-compactness-covering-embeddings", "thm-lc-supercompactness-closed-embedding-characterization", "def-lc-laver-anticipation-function", "lem-lc-fine-measure-coordinate-family"]}, {"convention": "A Laver anticipation function ℓ : κ → V_κ must anticipate every set x at every λ ≥ κ by a supercompactness embedding with j(ℓ)(κ) = x and ^λM ⊆ M, elementarity being a formula schema.", "fixed_by": "def-lc-laver-anticipation-function", "matters_for": ["thm-lc-laver-function-existence", "thm-lc-supercompact-preparation-interface"]}, {"convention": "Probability-algebra identity is measure-zero symmetric difference; order is μ(A∖B) = 0; m is strictly positive; completeness is for all set subsets.", "fixed_by": "lem-lc-probability-algebra-completeness", "matters_for": ["lem-lc-solovay-density-locality-and-null-joins", "lem-lc-generic-evaluation-of-measurable-densities", "lem-lc-solovay-measure-on-generic-subsets", "lem-lc-random-algebra-preserves-cardinals-and-sets-continuum", "lem-lc-random-coordinate-product-measure-pullback"]}, {"convention": "Real numbers are lower Dedekind cuts; h_G = {q ∈ ℚ : [{x : h(x) > q}] ∈ G}; the standard product measure on {0,1}^λ is the extension of the cylinder (not a larger Borel) sigma-algebra.", "fixed_by": "lem-lc-generic-evaluation-of-measurable-densities", "matters_for": ["lem-lc-solovay-measure-on-generic-subsets", "lem-lc-random-algebra-preserves-cardinals-and-sets-continuum", "lem-lc-random-coordinate-product-measure-pullback", "thm-lc-strong-compactness-product-measure-extension-interface"]}], "load_bearing": [{"id": "def-definable-subsets-of-a-membership-structure", "statement": "Def(A) = {{x ∈ A : (A,∈) ⊨ φ(x,a₁,…,aₙ)} : n < ω, a ∈ Aⁿ, FV(φ) ⊆ {v₀,…,vₙ}}, with Def(∅) = {∅} separately.", "used_by": ["lem-def-operation-is-absolute", "def-constructible-hierarchy-and-constructible-rank", "prop-constructible-levels-transitivity-ordinals-and-rank", "thm-separation-in-the-constructible-universe", "lem-canonical-well-order-of-finite-definition-codes", "ex-first-constructible-levels", "ex-definable-subsets-of-omega-are-not-all-subsets"]}, {"id": "def-forcing-names-and-name-rank", "statement": "P-names are recursively defined sets of pairs ⟨σ,p⟩ with p ∈ P and σ a name, stratified by N₀ = ∅, N_{α+1} = P(N_α × P), N_λ = ⋃_{β<λ}N_β, with rk_P(τ) = sup{rk_P(σ)+1 : ∃p ∈ P (⟨σ,p⟩ ∈ τ)}.", "used_by": ["lem-forcing-names-and-name-ranks-are-absolute", "def-forcing-name-valuation-and-generic-extension", "def-boolean-valued-name-semantics", "lem-boolean-valued-semantics-is-well-defined", "lem-lc-boolean-generic-truth"]}, {"id": "def-forcing-name-valuation-and-generic-extension", "statement": "val_G(τ) = {val_G(σ) : ∃p ∈ G (⟨σ,p⟩ ∈ τ)} and M[G] = {val_G(τ) : τ ∈ M a P-name} for a transitive ground M, with no genericity or ZF-satisfaction asserted.", "used_by": ["def-check-names-and-the-canonical-generic-name", "thm-check-name-evaluation-and-generic-reconstruction", "thm-generic-extension-transitivity-and-rank-bound", "lem-names-for-pairs-functions-and-ordinals", "lem-lc-boolean-generic-truth", "thm-lc-supercompact-preparation-interface"]}, {"id": "thm-rasiowa-sikorski-with-explicit-choice", "statement": "In ZFC, given nonempty P, dense sets (D_n)_{n<ω} and p ∈ P, a filter G ∋ p meets every D_n; with a supplied surjection e : ω → P the conclusion is provable in ZF.", "used_by": ["cor-generics-exist-over-countable-transitive-models", "fs-a-generic-filter-belongs-to-the-ground-model", "thm-lc-strong-compactness-product-measure-extension-interface"]}, {"id": "thm-lc-los-for-set-ultraproducts", "statement": "For every first-order φ, ∏_i M_i/U ⊨ φ([f₁],…,[f_n]) ⟺ {i : M_i ⊨ φ(f₁(i),…,f_n(i))} ∈ U; the diagonal map into an ultrapower is elementary.", "used_by": ["thm-lc-infinitary-los", "thm-lc-los-schema-for-universe-ultrapowers", "thm-lc-strong-compactness-fine-measures-and-logic"]}, {"id": "thm-lc-supercompactness-closed-embedding-characterization", "statement": "λ-supercompactness is equivalent to a definable elementary j : V → M with crit(j) = κ, j(κ) > λ and λ-sequential closure of M; the derived measure is U = {X ⊆ P_κ(λ) : j``λ ∈ j(X)}.", "used_by": ["cor-lc-large-cardinal-implication-ledger", "def-lc-laver-anticipation-function", "thm-lc-laver-function-existence", "thm-lc-supercompact-preparation-interface"]}, {"id": "thm-lc-laplace-placeholder-critical-point", "statement": "PLACEHOLDER-NOT-USED", "used_by": []}]}